  "body": "## Associated User Story\nAs an officer, I  want to be able to filter through all of the data on the point sheet.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n### Officers can see a point sheet dashboard and filter through any data type\n\n- Sunny: An officer opens the point sheet dashboard and filters through service points and is able to see all the members that have a service point or no service points depending on what filter they set.\n\n- Rainy: The filter for a “members with 0 service points” brings up members that actually have service points.\n\n\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied: \n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented; \n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes); \n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n\n## Evidence \n### Tests pass\n<img width=\"1132\" height=\"695\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-10-27 162923\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/16fc8330-17c7-4771-a984-dedededa15a3\" />\n\n### Rubocop\n<img width=\"867\" height=\"392\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-10-28 134017\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2582573e-7a42-4ff7-af47-7ea172fb56e2\" />\n\n",
